# SpecPlane

Default schema is v9.1.0. Follow `AGENTS.md`.

This repo has **two trees**: `specplane/` is the kit (language). `specs/` is the kernel product (what the CLI must do). Do not copy `specs/` into other apps. `design-docs/` is gitignored strategy, not specs.

For spec authoring, read `specplane/core_prompt/applicable/README.md` and load only the section for the current task. Do not attach `specplane_schema_prompt_v9.1.0.md` unless the user is changing the schema or explicitly asks for the complete reference.

Specs describe what and how well, not how. Keep bidirectional links in sync. Add a changelog entry when bumping `meta.version` on live 5C files.

Product requests in natural language use the change ritual in `specplane-implement` ([`docs/golden-journey.md`](docs/golden-journey.md)).

**PRE:** If the request could move a promise, `retrieve` before writing. If no live capability matches, do not open a change yet: offer two or three interpretations and the likely flows, and **wait**. Draft the spec from that choice and from ids `blast` already knows. After blast, classify reuse, extend, compose, or build (build last), and **wait** before code. Even a new component lists connections, constraints, and what not to duplicate. If retrieve hit, do not add a parallel capability or component for the same job. Typos/renames: no retrieve. If unsure, retrieve. Do not slurp the tree. Do not parse source in the kernel.

**POST:** After non-trivial work, `validate`, `check_sync --change <slug> --changed-ids`, then `run --change <slug>`. If this change already has a check, bind it (`run.unittest` or `run.argv`). Do not invent a test so SpecPlane has something to run. Do not parse `test_strategy`. Unbound `must:` is `not_run` on `run`, not a pass and not a certificate. Default check_sync (spec YAML in git only) is not a pass if you touched `tools/specplane/` or app code. Coverage pass is not behavioral agreement. `run` invokes bound checks only; it does not create tests or certify behavior. The kernel does not watch the chat.

Do not slurp `specs/`. Do not edit live YAML for in-flight work.
